## 5. Mixed Consistency Within One System

### Q: Can a single system use both consistency and availability for different features?

Yes — and this is the nuanced answer interviewers love. Real systems don't make one global choice; they make per-feature choices.

**Ticketmaster example:**

| Feature | Choice | Reason |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Booking a seat | Consistency | Double-booking is catastrophic |
| Viewing event details | Availability | Stale description for a few seconds is fine |
| Browsing available events | Availability | Slightly outdated availability count is acceptable |
| Payment processing | Consistency | Financial transactions must be accurate |

**Interview phrasing:** "For this ticketing system, I'll prioritize consistency for booking transactions but optimize for availability when users are browsing events."

**Tinder example:**

| Feature | Choice | Reason |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Match creation (both swipe right) | Consistency | Both users must see the match immediately |
| Viewing profiles | Availability | Slightly outdated photo is acceptable |
| Message delivery | Causal consistency | Messages must appear in order but slight delay is fine |

**Interview phrasing:** "For this dating app, I'll prioritize consistency for the matching logic but optimize for availability for profile viewing."

