## Final Mental Models

| Concept | Mental Model |
|---------|--------------|
| CAP theorem | A network split forces a binary choice: serve stale data or refuse to answer. |
| Partition tolerance | Not a choice — it's gravity. Networks will fail. |
| Strong consistency | Everyone reads from the same whiteboard, and the whiteboard is locked while someone writes. |
| Eventual consistency | A rumor spreading through a crowd — eventually everyone hears it, but not all at once. |
| Read-your-own-writes | You always see your own sticky notes immediately; others see them when they walk by your desk. |
| Causal consistency | A conversation where replies always come after the message they respond to — but unrelated chats have no guaranteed order. |
| Mixed consistency | A hospital: operating room is sterile (strong consistency), waiting room TV shows yesterday's news (eventual consistency). Same building, different standards. |

